# Loop: <LOOP_NAME>

> Declaration for one autonomous loop. Filled in with the human before the
> loop's first run. The autonomy level and change scope below are what the
> human is signing off on.

## Purpose
<One sentence: what this loop maintains or produces.>

## Pattern
<repo-health-audit | pr-guardian | dependency-patch-sweeper | custom>

## Autonomy level
- **Current:** L1        <!-- every new loop starts at L1 -->
- **Target:** <L1 | L2 | L3>
- **Promotion rule:** <default 5 consecutive clean runs, then a logged human decision>

## Change scope
- **Paths:** <allowlist, e.g. `docs/**`, `package-lock.json` — or "none (report-only)" at L1>
- **Change types:** <e.g. "patch-version bumps only"; "no deletions">
- **Granted outward actions:** <none | e.g. "open [prefix] issues, max N/run" — human-granted, logged>
- Anything outside this scope is **escalated, never done.**

## Rate limits
<e.g. max 3 PRs per run, one change per PR>

## Abort condition
<Rate limit exhausted | circuit-breaker trip | scope violation | failed verification.
 A scope violation always stops the run and escalates (runtime abort).
 Governance consequence: at L2/L3 demote one level; an L1 or repeated
 violation suspends the loop pending human review.>

## Cost circuit breaker
- **Ceiling:** <per-run spend ceiling, e.g. "$X" or "N tokens">
- **Record:** every run writes its actual spend to the state file at run end.
- **Read:** every re-entry reads that record first; over ceiling → stop + report.

## Verification (L2+)
<How an independent checker (separate context) validates each change before it
 becomes a PR. "no self-review".>

## Durable state file
- **Path:** <e.g. `LOOP-STATE.md`>
- Records: run history, attempts, blockers, and per-run spend.
- A fresh session re-enters by reading this file first.

## Schedule
- **Cadence (proposed):** <e.g. weekly>
- **Mechanism:** <cron | CI schedule | tool routine — installed by the human>
- Note: installing/changing the schedule is a human decision.

## Human gates (never automated)
- Merging
- Scope changes and deletions
- Outward-facing actions beyond the granted scope above
